# Claims. Long source quotations are deliberately avoided.
claim(1,[3,60],'the latter morphism is representable by unramified separated morphisms','For proper flat finitely presented X,Z/S, separated locally finitely presented Y/S and φ:Z→X, the formally unramified locus U of Hom(X,Y)→Hom(Z,Y) is open, and U→Hom(Z,Y) is scheme-representable, separated, unramified and locally finitely presented.','proof sketched','B','A-S01,04,08,10,12: modern reconstruction from Olsson Theorems1.1/1.5, the closed-section lemma, and Stacks0418. This bypasses the notebook’s incomplete Ext comparison.','Circulated by11 June1963; letter11 September1967; modern general algebraic-space route2006.','Established with the separated target and fp/flat/proper hypotheses. The original particular obstruction proof is not certified.',['Olsson2006','Stacks0418','BLR1990','Letter1963','Letter1967'],('targeted proof check','Checked hypothesis chain: proper-flat source gives Hom algebraic spaces; target separation gives closed diagonal via the closed-section criterion; on the tangent-injective open the map is unramified; Stacks0418 then yields schemes. See proof_notes.md §1.'),confidence='high')
claim(2,[3,5,60],'vérifier l’égalité des deux obstructions','Graph-ideal lift classes, scalar-change functoriality in Ext1, and their comparison with the class of compatible splittings are distinct obligations; lift sets are torsors only after nonemptiness is established.','open on the pages','C','A-S02,04: SGA3III Proposition4.2 verifies the quotient-lifting torsor mechanism; its hypotheses do not prove this particular naturality square or the existence used on scan18.','SGA3 seminar1963–1964, printed1970; current comparison19 November2026.','General deformation mechanism established; the exact two classes in these pages have not been identified term by term. Parameter multiplication also needs J-torsion-freeness.',['SGA3III'],('targeted proof check','Read the original and revised Proposition4.2 against the manuscript. Confirmed the formal-principal qualification; no claim of an Ext-comparison proof.'),'code/compute_a.py: regular_square_zero_ideal; outputs/compute_a.json',confidence='medium')
claim(3,[8],'il faut et suffit que λ(R1)=λ(R2)=0','For the displayed two-row module diagram, separate vanishing on σ(ker i) and σαπ′(ker β) is asserted sufficient for μi=λσ and μβ=λσαπ′. It is not sufficient in general.','false as stated','C','A-S01–04 sought the exact obstruction presentation; SGA3III supplies adjacent formalism, not this formula. The linear refutation and corrected universal presentation are CL-SA03-004.','Refuted in this run19 November2026; no priority assigned to the earlier-run counterexample.','False for the abstract diagram; it may hold with additional geometric relations not supplied on the page.',['SGA3III'],('refuted, with the refined statement\'s id','CL-SA03-004. One-dimensional exact rows, γ surjective, π′ a retraction: R1=R2=0 but μ=λ and μ=0 force λ=0.'),'code/compute_a.py: mixed_relation; outputs/compute_a.json')
claim(4,[8],'couples (μ,λ) compatibles','Editorial refinement: if q=(i,β):L⊕M′→M is onto and ρ=(σ,σαπ′), then compatible pairs are corepresented by coker(q,−ρ)≅J/ρ(ker q).','proof sketched','E','A-S01–04: the construction is the elementary pushout universal property; no claim that the corrected formula was written by Grothendieck or newly discovered here.','General module-category fact predates this notebook; exact historical first publication not assigned.','True for the fixed module diagram and arbitrary test modules. It does not establish that geometric corepresenting modules commute with arbitrary base change.',['SGA3III'],('independent re-proof','A linear map M⊕J→N annihilates (q,−ρ) exactly when its restrictions satisfy μq=λρ. Surjectivity of q eliminates M and leaves J/ρkerq; checked two finite examples.'),'code/compute_a.py: mixed_relation,coker_rho; outputs/compute_a.json')
claim(5,[8],'Coker ρ','The page’s replacement by cokerρ is asserted for compatible pairs. With q=ρ=id:k→k, compatible pairs form one copy of Hom(k,N), whereas cokerρ=0.','false as stated','C','A-S01–04; refined by CL-SA03-004. No exact literature endorsement of the erroneous displayed quotient located.','19 November2026 verification.','False as an abstract universal presentation; the pushout is the corrected formulation.',['SGA3III'],('refuted, with the refined statement\'s id','CL-SA03-004. The second one-dimensional test separates cokerρ from J/ρkerq.'),'code/compute_a.py: coker_rho; outputs/compute_a.json')
claim(6,[8],'J/(R1+R2) et changement de base plat','For a fixed module diagram, kernels, images and their finite sums commute with flat scalar extension, so J/(R1+R2) does too. A cokernel presentation itself commutes with every scalar extension.','proof sketched','E','A-S01–04: elementary exactness and right-exact tensor calculations; SGA3III uses the same pushout mechanism. No geometric base-change theorem is inferred.','Standard module algebra before the manuscript.','True in the fixed-diagram sense; does not repair CL003 or identify obstruction modules after nonflat base change.',['SGA3III'],('independent re-proof','Tensor the kernel-image sequences under flatness; for the corrected presentation use right exactness. These are different claims.'))
claim(7,[6],'Pb Simplifier … sans la propreté','Replacing properness by tangent restriction injectivity for every quasi-coherent coefficient would give formal unramifiedness; the text asks for a representability theorem under that replacement.','open on the pages','C','A-S01,04,08,10: Olsson1.5 retains properness; Stacks08K6 retains proper support for the coherent target. No source found establishing the proposed unrestricted removal.','Search completed19 November2026.','A precise additional finiteness/effectivity condition is missing; this run does not identify it as a currently open conjecture in the literature.',['Olsson2006','Stacks08K6','MOunramified'],('targeted proof check','Compared exact quantifiers with modern theorems. Formal unramifiedness and algebraicity are logically separate; page24 explicitly conditions its next construction on representing Hom modules.'),confidence='medium')
claim(8,[11],'Théorème … normalement plat le long de Zi','Let X/S be proper flat fp and P/X lfp. Suppose closed Zi⊂X are flat fp/S, the restrictions Res_Zi(P_Zi) are schemes, X is normally flat along Zi, and their union meets every geometric associated-point closure. The source asserts Res_X(P) is a scheme lfp/S.','stated without proof','C','A-S01,02,04,08,10: Olsson1.5 gives an algebraic space when P/X is separated fp; finite-source existence is BLR7.6/4. No exact published theorem with all the notebook’s quantifiers and unspecified target separation was located.','Announced in undated sheets; related Hom statement circulated1963 and1967; modern partial comparison2006.','Strong finite-probe formulation remains a reconstruction task, not declared unsolved mathematics. Its separation clause must be split off.',['Olsson2006','BLR1990','Letter1963','Letter1967'],('targeted proof check','Matched source hypotheses independently of later summaries and identified precisely the algebraic-space versus scheme and separation gaps.'),confidence='medium')
claim(9,[11],'un schéma … séparé?','The finite-probe theorem concludes separation with no visible separatedness assumption on P/X.','false as stated','C','A-S02,03,10: separatedness preservation requires separated target (BLR7.6/5(b)); corrected conditional statement is CL-SA03-010.','19 November2026 check.','If the doubtful word is really a separation assertion, the visible hypotheses are insufficient.',['BLR1990'],('refuted, with the refined statement\'s id','CL-SA03-010. Set X=S=Z=Spec k, P the affine line with doubled origin. X is proper flat fp and normally flat along itself; its only associated point is hit; Res_Z P=P exists, but it is not separated.'))
claim(10,[11,28],'séparé [hypothesis repair]','Editorial refinement: if P/X is separated and X/S is proper flat fp, the section functor, when algebraic, is separated over S.','proof sketched','B','A-S03,10: BLR7.6 Proposition2(ii) gives closed restriction of a closed immersion for proper flat fp source. Apply it to the diagonal of P/X.','BLR1990 exposition; underlying closed-section theorem already Murre1966 §3B.','Established; this repairs the separatedness clause without deciding the ink.',['BLR1990','Murre1966'],('targeted proof check','The diagonal of the section functor is the section functor of the equalizer closed in X; proper-flat closed-section representability gives a closed immersion.'))
claim(11,[11,21],'pour tout ouvert quasi-compact … quasi-affine','Under the finite-probe hypotheses and quasi-separated S, the text asserts that restriction from each quasi-compact open of Res_X P to ∏Res_Zi(P_Zi) is quasi-affine.','stated without proof','C','A-S01,02,04: exact normally-flat quasi-affine restriction statement not located in Murre, Olsson or BLR. Finite thickening methods explain a possible route, but fixed jet order is not uniformly faithful on all Hom components.','Search19 November2026.','Keep as a quantified manuscript claim; fixed-order jet counterexample refutes only an overstrong interpretation, not quasi-affineness.',['Murre1966','Olsson2006','BLR1990'],('targeted proof check','Checked the finite-jet test on P1: degree5 maps differing by ε z^3 agree to order3. A quasi-affine map need not be injective, so the theorem is not refuted.'),'code/compute_a.py: fixed_jet; outputs/compute_a.json',confidence='medium')
claim(12,[10,11],'essentiellement quasi-projectif; faisceau essentiellement ample','The source adds quasi-projectivity/essential ampleness for the section scheme under the indicated positivity of restrictions or suitable fibres meeting each associated-point closure.','stated without proof','C','A-S02,03,04: Ji Proposition2.10 proves the finite-flat quasi-projective-target case; it does not cover proper positive-dimensional source or the weaker fibrewise positivity condition.','Finite-source modern comparison2017; full claim search19 November2026.','The finite-source case is established; the exact broad fibrewise criterion is unlocated after the recorded search.',['Ji2017','BLR1990'],('targeted proof check','Compared the source’s associated-point quantifier with the finite-source positivity theorem; did not replace it by global quasi-projectivity.'),confidence='medium')
claim(13,[9,13],'sép. clos suffit; extension finie séparable','For proper X/k, enough radicial points in the required associated-point closures yield a scheme of sections; after a finite separable extension the source asserts the condition and representability. It also asserts a shrink-and-finite-étale variant over a noetherian integral base.','stated without proof','C','A-S01,04,06,08: the exact Hom corollaries already appear in the1963 letter; BLR and Olsson establish inputs. The finite-source smooth analogue is Bertapelle Theorem1.2. No exact published proof of every stated section/positivity refinement was located.','Circulation11 June1963; repeated11 September1967; finite-source smooth result arXiv7 June2016.','Historical claims securely identified. The algebraic-space conclusion is established; all stronger scheme/positivity clauses are not promoted together.',['Letter1963','Letter1967','Olsson2006','BLR1990','Bertapelle2016'],('targeted proof check','Distinguished fixed field extension from section-dependent jet order, and separated the generic shrinking step from descent of all components.'),confidence='medium')
claim(14,[15],'X has integral geometric fibers and a section along which X is smooth','The text asserts scheme representability for a smooth section with geometrically integral proper flat fibres; étale-local representability for geometrically reduced fibres; a further fpqf-local version without embedded associated cycles.','stated without proof','C','A-S04,06,08,10: both letters supply exact historical counterparts; Olsson1.5 supplies algebraic spaces with separated fp target. Stacks0A18 concerns connected components and does not by itself prove these scheme assertions.','1963 circulation;1967 repeat; modern comparison2006.','The smooth/reduced and no-embedded-cycle scopes remain distinct; the last fpqf generalization is not claimed settled by the references opened here.',['Letter1963','Letter1967','Olsson2006','Stacks0A18'],('targeted proof check','Read the three scopes and the changed topology. Geometric reducedness is not silently replaced by smoothness.'),confidence='medium')
claim(15,[16],'AutX/k is representable; the result holds too for Isom','For proper k-schemes X,Y, Aut_k(X) is a group scheme locally of finite type and Isom_k(X,Y) is a scheme.','stated without proof','B','A-S01,04,06,11: Matsumura–Oort1967 Theorem3.7 is the standard backward citation; metadata opened, original proof not read. Brion Theorem2.3 verifies the proper Aut formulation. Isom is a torsor when nonempty after a field extension and uses effective group-torsor descent.','Matsumura result reported in11 June1963 letter; journal1967.','Established; avoid confusing Aut with arbitrary Hom.',['MatsumuraOort1967','BrionAutos','Letter1963','Letter1967','Raynaud1968'],('used and rechecked in this run','The proper hypothesis and locally algebraic conclusion matched in the opened primary exposition; Isom reduction checked categorically. Original MO proof access limitation retained.'),confidence='high')
claim(16,[17],'plausible … prendre U′=U','For proper flat X over a noetherian integral S, the author asks whether shrinking alone makes Aut a scheme, eliminating a finite étale cover.','open on the pages','C','A-S03,06,11: Raynaud4.1 is an exact descent criterion, not an automatic affirmative answer; the unrestricted shrinking statement was not matched. Field Aut is CL015.','Search19 November2026; author pointer cf Raynaud undated.','Exact general claim unlocated; neither affirmed nor labelled an active modern open problem.',['Raynaud1968','MatsumuraOort1967','Olsson2006'],('targeted proof check','Checked that noetherian shrinking and eliminating an étale cover are separate from field representability.'),confidence='medium')
claim(17,[20],'if Y is quasi-projective … Hom is representable','Proper X/k and quasi-projective Y/k are asserted sufficient for Hom_k(X,Y) to be a scheme.','stated without proof','C','A-S01,04,11: exact assertion verified in1967 letter; Olsson1.1 gives an algebraic space. The opened finite-source quasi-projectivity results do not prove this positive-dimensional-source assertion.','Letter1967; algebraic-space theorem2006.','The statement is not contradicted; exact later proof was not located in the bounded search. Avoid equating it with the projective-source Hilbert-scheme theorem.',['Letter1967','Olsson2006','Ji2017'],('targeted proof check','Checked that the source says X proper, not projective; did not use Hilbert projective hypotheses that are absent.'),confidence='medium')
claim(18,[18],'Hom … not always representable … quadratic extension … proper non projective','The manuscript proposes a semilinear quadratic descent obstruction from a free involution and an orbit with no affine neighbourhood.','proof sketched','C','A-S01,03,11: Raynaud4.1 verifies the orbit-affine obstruction; Stacks08KE gives another effective-descent counterexample. The particular Nagata construction in these sheets remains unidentified; MO doubled-line example has a nonseparated target.','Letter1967; Raynaud seminar1967–1968.','The general obstruction is established; the source’s named proper example is not replaced by an inequivalent example.',['Raynaud1968','Stacks08KE','Letter1967','MOnonrep'],('targeted proof check','Checked the conditional orbit argument and the mismatch between a merely pointwise action and an actual trivial scheme action. No completed Nagata construction is claimed.'),confidence='medium')
claim(19,[19,28],'Hom(X,Y)=∏X/S(X×Y); products commute','Section restriction is right adjoint to base change; Hom_S(X,Y)=Res_X/S(X×_S Y), and Res_T/S X is the fibre over id_T of Hom_S(T,X)→Hom_S(T,T). Finite limits and group operations follow.','proved there','E','A-S03,05: BLR7.6 Lemma1 and Stacks05Y8 Lemma4 confirm the functor identities.','Formal adjunction fact predates the notebook; BLR1990 exposition.','True without representability assumptions at the functor level.',['BLR1990','Stacks05Y8'],('independent re-proof','Wrote the bijections on every test scheme; evaluated products/equalizers pointwise. This establishes only formal functor identities.'))
claim(20,[23],'descente: X0=f_*X×…f_*X','Given fpqc descent data on X/T, compatible sections are the equalizer of the two pullbacks to T×_S T. The written fibre-product formula requires the two maps and diagonal compatibility specified.','proof sketched','C','A-S03,05: BLR7.6 Proposition3 gives sheaf descent; Raynaud4.1 addresses geometric effectivity. The undeciphered immersion proviso prevents certification of the displayed scheme formula literally.','Classical descent; Raynaud1967–1968.','Functor equalizer is valid; representability and the exact fibre-product display remain conditional.',['BLR1990','Raynaud1968'],('independent re-proof','A compatible section obeys p2*s=descent(p1*s). Pulling to the diagonal identifies any redundant second section. This is an editorial clarification, not a decipherment.'),confidence='medium')
claim(21,[24],'f_*V̌(F)=V̌(f_*F)','For finite locally free f and finite-rank locally free F, V̌(F)=Spec Sym(F∨) represents sections and Res_f V̌(F)≅V̌(f_*F), with arbitrary base-change compatibility.','stated without proof','E','A-S03,05: BLR7.6 affine construction and Stacks0BL0 Lemma1. Finite rank is an explicit modern hypothesis; the source omits it.','Standard linear representation; comparison read19 November2026.','True with this bundle convention and finite rank; changing dual conventions changes the formula.',['BLR1990','Stacks0BL0'],('independent re-proof','For any R′, sections are Γ(T_R′,F_R′)=Γ(S_R′,(f_*F)_R′); affine finite pushforward and tensor commute.'))
claim(22,[25],'plus petit sous-faisceau …; les Mi tendent vers0 (?)','For proper flat X→Spec A, A complete noetherian local, coherent F and coherent K⊂f*F, a smallest submodule F1 with K⊂f*F1 exists. A decreasing family with zero module intersection has no nonzero coherent subobject in the pulled-back intersection.','proof sketched','C','A-S05,07,09,11: Chevalley module theorem located in inaccessible Hochster19.9; independent proof supplied. Stacks08K6 supports related coefficient representability but is not cited as an exact intersection theorem.','Complete-base result independently checked19 November2026; noncomplete opening not resolved.','True in the complete case by Chevalley cofinality, Krull intersection and proper support. Ordinary sheaf intersection need not vanish.',['ChevalleyNotes','Stacks08K6'],('independent re-proof','Proof_notes.md §3 proves the precise complete-base coherent-subobject statement and minimality. The identity morphism over k[[t]] refutes the raw sheaf-intersection alternative.'),confidence='high')
claim(23,[25],'f*(F1∩F2)=f*F1∩f*F2','Flat pullback preserves finite intersections of submodules; arbitrary intersections require a separate argument and a specified quasi-coherent infimum.','proved there','E','A-S05,07: standard exact-kernel calculation; the source explicitly invokes flatness.','Known exactness property before the manuscript.','True for finite intersections. The distinction from raw sheaf intersections is indispensable.',['Stacks08K6'],('independent re-proof','Express F1∩F2 as kernel(F1⊕F2→F) and tensor with the flat algebra; do not extend the argument to infinite products.'))
claim(24,[26],'Proposition2; Proposition2bis; plus grand ouvert','For finite locally free T/S and a family of opens Ui⊂X capturing the full image of every geometric section, representing Res Ui glue to represent Res X. The factorization locus in V is V minus the finite image of T_V\φ^{-1}(Ui).','proof sketched','B','A-S03,05: BLR7.6 Propositions2–3 and Theorem4; Stacks0BL0 Lemma3.','BLR1990; underlying construction earlier.','Established in the finite locally free case. Testing only finite residue extensions additionally needs the finite-presentation reduction.',['BLR1990','Stacks0BL0'],('independent re-proof','Checked the closed-image open locus and its arbitrary-base-change test via geometric fibres; overlaps are Res(Ui∩Uj), so sheaf gluing applies.'))
claim(25,[27],'f fini localement libre; radiciel; un ouvert affine','For finite locally free T/S, the finite-subset affine-neighbourhood criterion guarantees restriction is a scheme; a radicial source guarantees every section image lies in an affine neighbourhood.','stated without proof','B','A-S03,05: exact BLR7.6 Theorem4 and Stacks0BL0 Lemma3.','BLR1990 exposition.','Established; the radicial sentence’s cancellation is relocation, not a mathematical withdrawal.',['BLR1990','Stacks0BL0'],('targeted proof check','One geometric support point suffices in the radicial case; the open-locus argument promotes fibrewise containment to a neighbourhood.'))
claim(26,[28,29],'immersions fermées; ouverts; réunion sous hypothèse','Finite locally free restriction preserves affine morphisms, closed immersions and open immersions. Ordinary open covers need not restrict to covers unless every section image is captured in one member.','proof sketched','B','A-S03,05: BLR7.6 Proposition2; Ji Example4.1.','BLR1990; explicit modern example2017.','Preservation established; unqualified cover rule false and refined by CL024.',['BLR1990','Ji2017','Stacks0BL0'],('targeted proof check','Coefficient equations prove closed/affine cases; finite closed-image complement proves open case. Checked T=S⊔S, X=T, Ui the two components: ResX=S, both ResUi empty.'))
claim(27,[30],'propre; projectif [cas séparable]','Finite étale scalar restriction preserves proper and projective morphisms. Finite locally free restriction preserves relative quasi-projectivity under the existence assumptions.','proof sketched','B','A-S03,05: BLR7.6/5(f); Ji Propositions2.9–2.10.','BLR1990; Ji2017.','Established with the finite étale qualifier for properness/projectivity; the finite-flat generalization is false.',['BLR1990','Ji2017'],('targeted proof check','Étale-locally the source splits and restriction is a finite product. The nonsplit descent and projectivity step uses the cited positivity result; no assertion for arbitrary flat source.'))
claim(28,[31],'surjectif ⇒ f_*(g) surjectif','Unrestricted finite locally free restriction does not preserve surjections: Spec k→Spec k[ε]/ε² is surjective but has no section after any nonempty k-base change.','false as stated','C','A-S03,05: Ji Example4.9 and Proposition2.7 distinguish surjective from smooth surjective. Refined statement CL037.','Modern comparison2017; counterexample rerun19 November2026.','False without an extra lifting hypothesis; the source’s finite-étale Chow context may already supply one.',['Ji2017'],('refuted, with the refined statement\'s id','CL-SA03-037. The nilpotent ε must be both zero and the nonzero basis element in any putative section.'),'code/compute_a.py: surjectivity_failure; outputs/compute_a.json')
claim(29,[32],'fidèlement plat non fini … oui','Properness descends through fpqc base change; finiteness of the cover and a locally noetherian base are unnecessary.','open on the pages','B','A-S02,03: Stacks02L1, Lemma35.23.16.','Established modern fpqc descent; read19 November2026.','Affirmative with fpqc (or a covering family in that topology). The vague non-finite faithfully-flat phrase must still specify the covering condition.',['Stacks02L1'],('targeted proof check','Matched the precise fpqc-local-on-target assertion, not merely a nonfinite morphism.'))
claim(30,[33,34],'det f_*(L) ample, très ample','For finite locally free p, the normalized norm is det p*L⊗det p*O^{-1}; the omitted normalizing factor is pulled back from the base and does not alter relative ampleness. The source asserts ampleness/very ampleness after restriction.','proof sketched','B','A-S02,03,05: Stacks0BD2 norm formula; Ji2.10 supplies quasi-projectivity and norm-ampleness in its stated noetherian finite-flat setting. The universal very-ample claim is checked through the Grassmann construction, not identified with closedness.','BLR1990/Ji2017 comparisons.','Normalization correct; the established noetherian finite-flat positivity result is retained, and very ampleness means an immersion, not necessarily closed.',['Stacks0BD2','Ji2017'],('targeted proof check','Compared determinant transition functions; source-base tensor factor leaves relative ampleness unchanged. Grassmann Plücker line restricts to the determinant quotient line.'))
claim(31,[34],'immersion projective fermée','The proposed projective embedding of Res(P^n) is asserted closed for arbitrary finite locally free source.','false as stated','C','A-S03,05: Ji2.10 proves quasi-projectivity, not properness; refined locally-closed construction CL032.','19 November2026 verification.','False: over dual numbers Res(P1) is the tangent bundle of P1; its closed affine-line fibre prevents properness.',['Ji2017'],('refuted, with the refined statement\'s id','CL-SA03-032. The dual-number first-order expansion identifies the restriction with T(P1); a closed subscheme of projective space would be proper.'),'code/compute_a.py: P1_tangent_restriction; outputs/compute_a.json')
claim(32,[35],'φ_iλμ=0; det(uξ) inversible','For finite free B/A, the B-stability locus of an A-locally free quotient of B^n is closed in the ordinary Grassmannian. The locus where the quotient is B-locally free of fixed rank is open; together they realize the restriction as a locally closed subscheme.','proof sketched','B','A-S03,05: compared with Ji2.10 and BLR affine coefficient constructions; the exact universal equations are independently verified here.','Modern formulations established; handwritten calculation independently checked19 November2026.','Valid scheme-theoretically, including nonreduced tests; the open B-freeness condition is essential.',['Ji2017','BLR1990'],('independent re-proof','Stability is vanishing of B⊗kernel→quotient; local cyclic/free generators are detected by determinants. In a dual-number chart stability gives M²=0, and freeness is an open cyclic-determinant condition.'),'code/compute_a.py: grassmann_stability_freeness; outputs/compute_a.json')
claim(33,[36],'de type fini; rédiger convenablement','With locally noetherian S, finite locally free T/S and finite-type X/T satisfying the affine-image representability criterion, restriction is finite type.','proof sketched','B','A-S03,05: BLR7.6 Proposition5(a,c,e); Ji2.5.','BLR1990.','Established with the stated hypotheses; noetherianness is only used in the manuscript’s finite-cover route, not asserted optimal.',['BLR1990','Ji2017'],('independent re-proof','On noetherian affine S of constant rank d>0, ⋃Ui^d is a quasi-compact open in X^d; finitely many Ui capture all support tuples of size≤d by repetitions. Rank0 gives the terminal scheme.'))
claim(34,[37],'dimension zéro … f_*X de dimension>0','Without smoothness, a zero-dimensional finite-source target can have positive-dimensional restriction. Dual-number endomorphisms are Spec k[a,b]/(a²,2ab).','proof sketched','B','A-S03,05: Ji’s smooth dimension theorem cannot be applied to this nonsmooth example; direct equations verify the source’s surviving dimension warning. The explicit dual-number choice is deleted in the manuscript and supplied by the prior run.','19 November2026 computation; no novelty claim.','True warning; characteristic2 changes the nilpotent translation structure and must not be dropped.',['Ji2017'],('computation or formal certificate','Expanded (a+bε)² modulo ε² and retained both a² and2ab. For char≠2, b invertible forces a=0, giving Gm as automorphism locus.'),'code/compute_a.py: dual_number_endomorphism; outputs/compute_a.json')
claim(35,[40],'T/S affine … g lisse ⇒ f_*g lisse','When T/S is affine, g:X→Y is smooth, and the restriction morphism is represented and locally finitely presented, restriction is smooth.','proof sketched','B','A-S03,05: BLR7.6/5(h) and Ji2.6(6) establish the finite-locally-free case; the broader affine-source conditional assertion follows from formal smoothness on affine tests.','Established finite-source comparison1990; broader conditional proof checked2026.','True with existence and lfp made explicit. Dropping affineness loses global smooth lifting in this argument.',['BLR1990','Ji2017'],('independent re-proof','A square-zero affine base test pulls back to an affine T-scheme; a smooth morphism has a global lift there, since the local lifts form a quasi-coherent torsor. Lfp plus formal smoothness yields smoothness.'))
claim(36,[40,41],'g étale ⇒ f_*g étale','Given representability and lfp, restriction of an étale morphism is étale; here no affineness of T/S is needed for the formal-lifting argument.','proof sketched','B','A-S03,05: Stacks02HF unique lifting and local gluing; Stacks05Y8 Lemma3 gives finite locally free case.','Modern references read19 November2026.','True; the source’s one-point uniqueness and numerical-bound proof is unnecessary and needs separation.',['Stacks02HF','Stacks05Y8'],('independent re-proof','Étale lifts exist locally and are unique, so glue over arbitrary pullback T; lfp supplies the étale conclusion.'))
claim(37,[47],'g lisse surjectif; T/S fini','If T/S is finite locally free and g is smooth surjective, represented restriction is smooth surjective; a represented smooth torsor restricts to a torsor under the restricted group.','proof sketched','B','A-S03,05: Ji2.7 and5.6; finite-limit identity plus local smooth sections supplies the torsor conclusion.','Ji2017; backward CGP reference not directly opened.','Established for finite source. The conflicting scan55 finite/sans-fini readings cannot extend the assertion.',['Ji2017','BLR1990'],('targeted proof check','Over algebraically closed residue fields T is a finite product of Artin local rings; choose smooth-fibre points and lift across the nilpotent ideals. This proves surjectivity on geometric points.'))
claim(38,[41],'known by image of one point; at most n^ν sections','One-point determination and the bound n^ν for arbitrary nonseparated étale g over a connected affine source are asserted in the proof.','false as stated','C','A-S03,05: Stacks024V Proposition41.6.3 explicitly includes separatedness. The valid étale conclusion is CL036.','19 November2026 test.','False without separation: the doubled line at0 and1 has four sections, largest fibre2 and ν=1.',['Stacks024V','Stacks02HF'],('refuted, with the refined statement\'s id','CL-SA03-036. Four independent branch choices give the constant four-point section scheme; all standing affine/finite-type/étale conditions are satisfied.'),'code/compute_a.py: nonseparated_etale; outputs/compute_a.json')
claim(39,[42],'D(s)=nD′(s)','The literal dimension-set identity for smooth restriction, and the naive repair D′=nD for mixed dimensions, both fail.','false as stated','C','A-S03,05: Ji Corollary3.8 has pure dimension; refinement CL040.','19 November2026.','Literal equation is reversed; mere reversal does not fix mixed or section-invisible components.',['Ji2017'],('refuted, with the refined statement\'s id','CL-SA03-040. Dual-number A1 gives D={1},D′={2},n=2. Split source with target dimensions{1,2} gives{2,3,4}, not{2,4}.'),'code/compute_a.py: mixed_dimensions,dual_number_affine_dimension; outputs/compute_a.json')
claim(40,[42,43],'si g lisse de dim pure d … nd','For finite locally free T/S of rank n and smooth g of pure relative dimension d, a represented restriction has pure relative dimension nd. At an individual section the general dimension is the sum of local source lengths times the target dimensions encountered by that section.','proof sketched','B','A-S03,05: Ji Corollary3.8 proves the field-algebra case; affine smooth charts and geometric fibres give the relative formulation.','2017 exposition; earlier standard result, first occurrence not determined.','Established. The dimensions of components not admitting a section contribute nothing.',['Ji2017','BLR1990'],('independent re-proof','At a geometric section, tangent space is Γ(T_s,section*Tang_g), of dimensionΣ length(Bj)d_j. Smoothness converts tangent dimension into fibre dimension. Pure d gives nd.'),'code/compute_a.py: mixed_dimensions,dual_number_affine_dimension; outputs/compute_a.json')
claim(41,[44],'exactement λ^ν points','For finite locally free T/S and finite étale g of constant degreeλ, the geometric fibre of Res g has λ^ν_s points, ν_s=#π0(T_sbar).','proof sketched','B','A-S03,05,08: finite Artin local decomposition plus topological invariance; compare Bertapelle Theorem1.2 for smooth component sets.','Modern comparison2016/2017; direct check2026.','Correct for finite source. Rank n (length) and ν (component count) serve different roles.',['Stacks04DY','Bertapelle2016'],('independent re-proof','Each strictly local Artin component has exactlyλ sections of a degreeλ finite étale cover, and choices over the ν components are independent.'),'code/compute_a.py: finite_etale_counts; outputs/compute_a.json')
claim(42,[44],'fini [deleted] … λ^ν','The same degree formula with no source finiteness does not follow from affine finite type and connected source.','false as stated','C','A-S03,05,08: all opened degree theorems retain finite source. Corrected statement CL041.','19 November2026.','False: over algebraically closed char≠2, squaring Gm→Gm has no section although its finite étale degree is2 and Gm has one component; the section functor is empty.',['Stacks04DY','BLR1990'],('refuted, with the refined statement\'s id','CL-SA03-041. Units in K[t,t^-1] are c t^m, so a square root of t would require2m=1. Any nonempty test base has a geometric point, excluding every section.'),'code/compute_a.py: nonfinite_source_degree_formula; outputs/compute_a.json')
claim(43,[45],'Conditions équivalentes … homogène','For finite locally free T/S: locally constant ν_s; preservation of finite étale morphisms; finite étale restriction of every finite étale T-object; and finiteness of Res(T⊔T), are equivalent.','stated without proof','B','A-S06,08,12: exact title terminology not located; the assertion follows from Stacks04DY and finite-source étale preservation, with a complete independent proof in proof_notes.md §4.','Independent check19 November2026; first publication under this terminology not established.','Established in the finite locally free scope. The binary finiteness condition is already sufficient because that restriction is étale.',['Stacks04DY','Stacks05Y8','BLR1990'],('independent re-proof','Étale-locally constant ν splits T into finite flat universal homeomorphisms; use topological invariance. Conversely binary rank2^ν detects ν. All implications and arbitrary-base-change compatibility checked.'))
claim(44,[45],'stable par changement de base; composition [cas fini]','The finite locally free homogeneous class is stable under arbitrary base change and composition.','stated without proof','B','A-S06,12: combine CL043 with composition of restriction right adjoints; no exact historical terminology match located.','19 November2026 verification.','True for the finite class; source’s broader deleted-finite scope is not included.',['Stacks04DY','BLR1990'],('independent re-proof','Base change preserves geometric ν and restriction; composition preserves finite étale objects because each of the two right adjoints does.'))
claim(45,[46,47],'ν_s; f_*(T×G)','Restricted constant finite group G has geometric group G^{ν_s}; homogeneity gives finite étale local constancy, while length n governs smooth affine dimension.','proof sketched','B','A-S03,06,08,12: finite-limit formalism, CL041/043 and Bertapelle Theorem1.2 are exact compatible inputs.','Modern component comparison2016; check2026.','True under the specified finite-source hypotheses. For μ2/Z2 the binary restriction is étale but not finite.',['Bertapelle2016','Stacks04DY','BLR1990'],('computation or formal certificate','Computed idempotents a+bx of Z2[x]/(x²−1): a²+b²=a,2ab=b; four generic geometric solutions, two special ones. This is a test of varying ν, not an arithmetic-project result.'),'code/compute_a.py: mu2_binary_test,finite_etale_counts; outputs/compute_a.json')
claim(46,[49],'Hom̲_S(A,E)=Hom̲_S(T,E); T→A','For finite locally free homogeneous T/S there is a finite étale component quotient A(T), with T→A(T) a finite locally free universal homeomorphism on each local component and internal Hom_S(A(T),E)≅internal Hom_S(T,E) for finite étale E, compatibly with every base change.','proof sketched','B','A-S06,08,12: CL043’s local splitting constructs A; Stacks04DY proves the internal universal property. Bertapelle Theorem1.2 concerns geometric component sets and is compatible but not identical.','Independent modern reconstruction2026; source continues atscan59.','True in this precise finite homogeneous setting. Global ordinary-Hom corepresentability alone is weaker.',['Stacks04DY','Bertapelle2016'],('independent re-proof','Glue component labels over étale trivializations. Universal homeomorphism invariance proves the Hom property after arbitrary test-base pullback; uniqueness gives descent of A.'))
claim(47,[50],'un tel foncteur est nécessairement … Hom̲π1(A,E)','A left-exact endofunctor of finite π1-sets need not be internal Hom by a fixed finite π1-set.','false as stated','C','A-S06,08,12 sought the equivariant formulation; precise geometric replacement CL046. The false general categorical premise is independently tested.','19 November2026.','False even with finite-colimit and surjection preservation: forget a C2-action and put the trivial action on the same set.',['Stacks04DY','Bertapelle2016'],('refuted, with the refined statement\'s id','CL-SA03-046. Evaluation at the trivial two-element set forces|A|=1; then exponentiation is identity, but the regular C2-action is changed by F.'),'code/compute_a.py: C2_internal_Hom_counterexample; outputs/compute_a.json')
claim(48,[54],'closed section functor iff compatible with adic limits','For flat finite-type X/S over locally noetherian S and closed Y⊂X, the subfunctor of S where Y_T=X_T is a closed subscheme exactly when the adic-effectivity condition holds; proper X supplies it.','proof sketched','B','A-S01,03,04: Murre §3B Theorem3 and corollary; SGA3VIII6.4 supplies another sufficient condition (essential freeness).','Murre talkMay1965, print1966; source sheet undated.','Established closed-immersion version. Monomorphism/immersion and nonnoetherian margin variants are not bundled into it.',['Murre1966','SGA3VIII','BLR1990'],('targeted proof check','Matched flatness, finite type, locally noetherian base and closed target to the actual printed statement.'))
claim(49,[55],'Condition R … centralisateurs, transporteurs, normalisateurs','For flat locally finite-type H satisfying the source’s R condition over locally noetherian S, centralizers and transporters into G are asserted representable, with closedness for separated G; normalizers follow with the written subgroup hypotheses.','proof sketched','C','A-S01,03,06,07: Murre §3B group application and SGA3VIII6.4–6.7 give exact closed-section/essential-free counterparts. No equivalence of every R variant with essential freeness is asserted.','SGA3 seminar1963–1964/print1970; Murre1966.','Established under SGA3 essential freeness and separation; exact R/DVR reductions remain to be checked.',['Murre1966','SGA3VIII'],('targeted proof check','Transporter equations are pulled-back diagonal conditions; the printed theorem needs essential freeness. The manuscript’s connected-fibre and DVR formulations are recorded without a silent equivalence.'),confidence='medium')
claim(50,[56],'foncteur d’aplatissement représentable iff adic condition','For coherent E on finite-type X over locally noetherian S, the flattening subfunctor is represented by an unramified locally finite-type monomorphism iff the stated adic limit condition holds; proper X supplies effectivity.','proof sketched','B','A-S01,03,04: Murre §3A Theorem2 and Corollary1.','MurreMay1965 talk/1966 print.','Established proper coherent flattening statement. Faithful-flat and group/R extensions require their own nonempty-support conditions.',['Murre1966','Stacks08K6'],('targeted proof check','Compared coherent sheaf flatness with source-scheme flatness; did not identify the doubtful F_T with E_T by changing the source.'))
claim(51,[57],'pr1:X×_S X→X plat iff factorisation plate puis monomorphisme','For finitely presented X→S, flatness of the self-relation projection is asserted equivalent to a unique factorization X→S′→S with first map faithfully flat and second a finitely presented monomorphism.','proof sketched','B','A-S01,03: Murre §3A Corollary2 is the locally noetherian finite-type counterpart; limit arguments give the fp formulation when the construction descends.','MurreMay1965/1966.','Published counterpart identified. This run checks the locally noetherian theorem; the arbitrary-base approximation is a stated scope extension, not a newly certified proof.',['Murre1966'],('targeted proof check','Both directions and uniqueness of the quotient sheaf compared to the printed corollary; checked the manuscript’s later proof continuation rather than stopping at Reste.'),confidence='medium')
claim(52,[58],'P formellement principal homogène devient un fibré principal','A formal principal-action isomorphism P×G≅P×P is claimed sufficient for an fppf torsor over a unique monomorphism S′→S, without a visible flatness assumption on G.','false as stated','C','A-S01,03,06: Murre flat-self-relation criterion requires flatness of that projection. Correct conditional result CL053.','19 November2026 test.','Without inherited G-flatness the statement fails; no decision is made whether the missing hypothesis was tacit on another sheet.',['Murre1966'],('refuted, with the refined statement\'s id','CL-SA03-053. G=P=Spec k[t,x]/(tx) has translation principal-action isomorphism and a section but is not flat overk[t]; a factoring monomorphism S′ must beS.'),'code/compute_a.py: nonflat_principal_action; outputs/compute_a.json')
claim(53,[58],'formal principal homogeneous [flatness refinement]','Editorial repair: for flat finitely presented G/S and finitely presented P/S with P×G≅P×P, the flat-self-relation theorem supplies a unique support monomorphism S′→S and an fppf G_S′-torsor P→S′.','proof sketched','B','A-S01,03: direct application of Murre §3A Corollary2, followed by the principal-action identity.','Murre1966 input; explicit refinement2026.','True in the locally noetherian finite-presentation scope checked here.',['Murre1966'],('independent re-proof','P×G→P is flat fp; transfer by the action isomorphism to P×P→P, apply factorization, and retain the torsor identity after base change.'))
claim(54,[59],'Ker u plat … G/N existe','For a finitely presented homomorphism u:G→H with flat finitely presented kernel N, the fppf image quotient G/N is a scheme, a monomorphism into H.','proof sketched','B','A-S01,03: the application immediately after Murre §3A Corollary2 verifies this in the locally noetherian finite-type setting.','Murre1966.','Established published counterpart; arbitrary-base extensions need the same approximation qualification as CL051.',['Murre1966'],('targeted proof check','G×_H G≅G×N; kernel flatness supplies the previous self-relation criterion. Quotient here is the image of the given map, not an arbitrary group quotient.'),confidence='medium')
claim(55,[60],'Hom(w*Ω,G)=Hom(M_w,G); Nakayama','For proper flat fp source and coherent finite-presentation E, the linear functor G↦Hom(E,f*G) is corepresented locally by a coherent module compatible with base change. Surjectivity of the tangent-module map defines an open locus.','proof sketched','B','A-S04,08: Stacks08JY and08K6, with explicit backward comparison to EGAIII Cor7.7.8, verify coherent Hom representability. The notebook’s duality direction is checked using Hom(−,G).','EGAIII1963 backward reference; modern Stacks read2026.','Established; injective/surjective transcription conflict must be resolved on scans.',['Stacks08JY','Stacks08K6'],('targeted proof check','Coherent cokernel support is closed and Nakayama detects fibrewise surjectivity. Contravariance of Hom reverses the tangent-arrow direction.'))
claim(56,[55,56],'condition R: réduction aux traits; hypothèses non noethériennes','The source proposes testing R by DVRs, gives connected-fibre and finite-subscheme-cover sufficient conditions, and sketches nonnoetherian or merely unramified extensions of its criteria.','open on the pages','C','A-S03,06,07: SGA3VIII6.1–6.4 supplies essential freeness and its base-change/descent properties. No source opened proves all the notebook R equivalences or the nonnoetherian generalization as worded.','Search19 November2026.','Partial established framework; the exact equivalences are unlocated, not declared disproved.',['SGA3VIII','Murre1966'],('targeted proof check','Separated the live finite-type local-base condition from cancelled formulations and from the essentially-free theorem.'),confidence='medium')

