problem(1,'Existence and comparison of compatible infinitesimal lifts',[3,60],'Supply a lift before using the torsor square and prove the two Ext obstruction classes equal, naturally under coefficient change.','Use the graph-ideal deformation problem with its cotangent/Ext data and verify every comparison map; alternatively use CL001’s algebraic-space proof for the theorem itself.','SGA3III4.2 proves a formal-principal quotient-lift mechanism; Olsson1.1/1.5 plus Stacks0418 proves the separated relative representability conclusion.','Scans19–23 expose existence and equality as separate missing checks; no external source explains a later abandonment.','Worth a focused reconstruction because it distinguishes a correct theorem from a flawed handwritten route.',['SGA3III','Olsson2006','Stacks0418'])
problem(2,'Remove properness from the Hom criterion',[6],'Replace properness by tangent injectivity for all quasi-coherent coefficients.','Require a separately proved algebraicity/effectivity theorem or proper support; formal unramifiedness alone is insufficient.','Olsson1.5 retains proper flat fp source; Stacks08K6 requires proper support of its flat coherent target. No exact unrestricted result located in A-S01,04,08,10.','The author calls this Pb and later assumes the Hom modules are representable; nothing in the searched sources states why it was dropped.','Worth a bounded hypothesis audit before any attempt at a general theorem.',['Olsson2006','Stacks08K6'])
problem(3,'The mixed relation and quotient presentation',[8],'Find the module representing compatible splittings and justify the two relations and base change.','Use C=coker(q,−ρ)=J/ρ(ker q); prove any extra geometric condition needed to replace mixed relations by separate kernels.','CL003 andCL005 are refuted by exact computations; CL004 is the universal pushout formula. SGA3III4.2 is adjacent deformation formalism, not a proof of the manuscript simplification.','The source switches between two quotients without supplying the missing relation argument.','Worth developing because a short diagram audit can identify whether the geometric special case repairs the abstract error.',['SGA3III'])
problem(4,'Finite probes and normal flatness',[11,21],'Prove the scan26 scheme-representability theorem and the quasi-affine map on quasi-compact opens.','State target separation and fp hypotheses, construct higher infinitesimal probes with flatness, and allow probe order to vary with bounded families of maps.','Olsson1.5 gives algebraic spaces; BLR7.6/4 gives finite-source schemes. The exact normally-flat quantitative theorem was not located (A-S01,02,04,08,10).','No proof follows the announcement; fixed-order jets do not determine all infinitesimal Hom maps.','High-value reconstruction after the source’s ambiguous hypotheses are checked on scans.',['Olsson2006','BLR1990','Letter1963'])
problem(5,'Essential ampleness from associated-point fibres',[10,11],'Construct an essentially ample line bundle when suitable fibres of P are quasi-projective in every associated-point closure.','First prove the finite-source norm/Grassmannian case; then specify exactly how the finite probes and positivity descend to each quasi-compact Hom open.','Ji2.10 proves the finite-flat quasi-projective-target case; no exact fibrewise refinement of this proper-source theorem was matched.','The source gives a marginal strengthening without construction; no cause of historical omission is documented.','Worth a separate run because its quantifiers are stronger than the standard quasi-projective-target result.',['Ji2017','BLR1990'])
problem(6,'Are connected components of Hom finite type?',[12],'Are connected components of the section scheme over a field of finite type?','There is no positive theorem in this generality; formulate bounded strata or impose an ample polarization and a fixed Hilbert polynomial.','Ji Example6.5 pp18–19 gives a proper-target degree-doubling counterexample; SchwedeCor3.7 provides the gluing existence input. The literal lft-target statement already fails for X=Spec k and a connected non-quasi-compact lft scheme.','The1963 letter explicitly says the method does not solve the question and suspects a negative answer; later negative examples explain the boundary, not his personal decision.','Worth annotating with the precise counterexample, not reopening as an unqualified conjecture.',['Ji2017','Schwede2005','Letter1963'])
problem(7,'Uniform field extension and spreading out',[13,14],'Choose a finite separable field extension, and over an integral noetherian base shrink and pass to a finite étale cover, to obtain representability.','Separate one extension depending on source geometry from a jet order depending on a map or quasi-compact family.','The1963 and1967 letters state the Hom version; Olsson1.1 and BLR7.6/4 establish major inputs, but the full section/positivity refinements were not matched.','Deleted margins ask about quasi-compactness and target finite type; they are not a retraction of the live corollaries.','Worth checking within the finite-probe reconstruction, not as a separate novelty claim.',['Letter1963','Letter1967','Olsson2006','BLR1990'])
problem(8,'Smooth sections, reduced fibres, and fpqf locality',[15],'Pass from a smooth section to geometrically reduced fibres and then to fpqf locality without embedded associated cycles.','Keep the three settings separate and specify source/target separation, finite presentation and topology.','Olsson1.5 establishes algebraic-space representability; the letters verify the historical scheme claims. Stacks0A18 only gives a component-constancy input.','The author changes topology and removes hypotheses in successive short corollaries; no complete transition proof is written.','Worth a targeted proof audit after the exact corollary indices and simple/type-finite readings are checked.',['Letter1963','Letter1967','Olsson2006','Stacks0A18'])
problem(9,'Can the Aut étale cover be omitted?',[17],'After shrinking a noetherian integral base, take U′=U in the automorphism representability corollary.','Prove scheme effectivity for this group algebraic space on a common nonempty open, including all components.','Matsumura–Oort gives the field theorem; Raynaud4.1 gives an orbit-affine criterion. No exact general shrinking statement was identified.','The only authorial explanation is plausible and cf Raynaud; no later abandonment reason was found.','Worth a literature-focused run on group algebraic spaces, with no assumption that generic representability automatically spreads uniformly.',['MatsumuraOort1967','Raynaud1968'])
problem(10,'Identify the Nagata quadratic Hom counterexample',[18],'Turn the orbit-without-affine-neighbourhood construction into a lemma and complete the unfinished condition on K.','Specify an actual proper separated nonprojective scheme with an involution and semilinear descent datum, then apply the orbit criterion.','Raynaud4.1 is the exact descent criterion; Stacks08KE is a different example; the1967 letter asserts the quadratic proper-target failure.','The first argument is crossed out, the replacement requests details, and the final sentence is unfinished.','Worth a source-and-construction run because substituting a doubled nonseparated line misses the claimed strength.',['Raynaud1968','Stacks08KE','Letter1967','MOnonrep'])
problem(11,'Clarify the descent fibre product',[23],'Specify the maps and immersion-type proviso in the formula for X0.','Use the fpqc equalizer of compatible sections, then prove geometric representability under an explicit descent criterion.','BLR7.6/3 handles sheaf descent; Raynaud4.1 separates effectivity from formal compatibility.','The proviso is difficult to read and the two maps are not fully labelled.','Worth a short diagram reconstruction only after the scan is checked.',['BLR1990','Raynaud1968'])
problem(12,'Smallest coherent envelope and infinite intersections',[25],'Show the coherent submodule envelope exists and that a decreasing family tends to zero; distinguish ordinary intersection from quasi-coherent infimum.','For complete noetherian local A prove the coherent-subobject statement as in CL022; then separately descend the envelope if the opening base is merely local noetherian.','Independent complete-base proof is in proof_notes §3; Stacks08K6 provides related proper-support Hom theory. Hochster19.9 was located but not opened successfully.','The page itself weakens raw sheaf vanishing and asks about cofinality; Pro and Codex disagree on the complete hypothesis.','Worth a compact run on the noncomplete descent step after resolving that reading.',['Stacks08K6','ChevalleyNotes'])
problem(13,'Finite residue-field tests and gluing',[26,27],'Make the incomplete finite-extension reduction and gluing proof precise.','Use geometric section images, their maximal open factorization loci, and finite presentation when replacing arbitrary residue extensions by finite ones.','BLR7.6/2–4 and Stacks0BL0 Lemma3 prove the finite-source construction; later scans70–77 repeat the open-locus and finite-support arguments.','The first proof stops at Il provient donc; the next proposition changes the existence assumption and supplies the gluing route.','Useful editorial completion, largely established mathematics rather than a new research problem.',['BLR1990','Stacks0BL0'])
problem(14,'Proper/projective preservation and the Chow route',[30,31],'Detail proper/projective restriction in the separable case and the use of surjective covers.','Retain finite étale source for properness/projectivity; use smooth surjectivity or an appropriate finite-étale splitting argument, not bare surjectivity.','BLR7.6/5(f) and Ji2.7,2.9–2.10 give the precise boundaries; CL028 supplies the nilpotent counterexample.','The page marks the Chow argument for detailed verification and adds finiteness/noetherian qualifications.','Useful to complete the commentary; the arbitrary finite-flat properness statement is already false.',['BLR1990','Ji2017'])
problem(15,'Properness under nonfinite faithfully flat descent',[32],'Does properness descend when the faithfully flat cover is not finite?','Yes for fpqc covers, without noetherian assumptions.','Stacks02L1 Lemma35.23.16 is exact.','The page answers yes under locally noetherian hypotheses; no unresolved modern obstacle remains in the fpqc formulation.','No new development needed; record the sharper established theorem and the topology condition.',['Stacks02L1'])
problem(16,'Determinant ampleness versus closed embedding',[33,34],'Verify determinant ampleness/very ampleness and the proposed projective closed immersion.','Normalize the norm, retain immersion rather than closed immersion for general finite-flat source, and separate finite-étale properness.','Stacks0BD2 gives the norm; Ji2.10 proves finite-source quasi-projectivity; the tangent-bundle example refutes the excess closedness.','The subsequent Grassmannian construction deletes fermé and introduces an open freeness locus.','Worth documenting the exact correction; no research should try to prove the false closedness claim.',['Stacks0BD2','Ji2017'])
problem(17,'Scheme-theoretic Grassmannian equations',[35],'Detail the B-stability equations, denominator clearing and open local-freeness condition.','Work with the universal quotient and the map B⊗kernel→quotient; use determinant opens of local B-bases.','CL032 independently verifies the equations, including a dual-number chart; Ji2.10 provides the comparison.','The margin explicitly asks to préciser conditions de validité.','A short editorial proof can finish this portion without new theory.',['Ji2017','BLR1990'])
problem(18,'Finite support-cover argument',[36],'Write the X^ν noetherian finite-subcover argument carefully.','Reduce to constant finite rank over a noetherian affine base, allow repeated support points, and treat rank0 separately.','BLR7.6/5(a,c,e) is the established finiteness result; later scan77 states the finite-subfamily lemma.','The source says rédiger convenablement and revises quasi/finiteness wording.','No open theorem remains under the stated hypotheses; useful as a concise completed proof.',['BLR1990','Ji2017'])
problem(19,'Smooth lifting after dropping finiteness',[40],'Prove restriction preserves smoothness after replacing finite source by an affine source.','Require the represented restriction map to be locally finitely presented and use affine square-zero lifting.','BLR7.6/5(h) verifies finite source; CL035 independently checks the conditional affine-source formulation.','The author inserts affine specifically in the smooth clause, while transcriptions differ on the deleted finite assumption.','Worth clarifying the statement, but the conditional lifting argument is complete.',['BLR1990','Ji2017'])
problem(20,'One-point determination and the section bound',[41],'Justify determining a lift from one point and the bound n^ν.','Add separatedness, connected components and equality on residue-field maps; do not use this bound to prove the already valid étale theorem.','Stacks024V Proposition41.6.3 supplies the separated uniqueness result; CL038’s doubled-two-point example refutes the unqualified bound.','The source’s proof uses uniqueness not guaranteed by the stated étale hypothesis.','No need to pursue the false general bound; retain the clean unique-lifting proof of étaleness.',['Stacks024V','Stacks02HF'])
problem(21,'Repair the smooth dimension statement',[42,43],'Resolve D versus D′ and prove the pure-dimensional nd corollary.','Use the length-weighted dimension sum along each actual section; pure dimension d gives nd.','Ji Corollary3.8 proves the finite field-algebra version; CL039–040 give exact tests and the tangent proof.','The written formula and following sentence disagree, and mixed dimensions create a second mathematical issue beyond the typographical reversal.','A short corrected statement is worthwhile; avoid the false scalar set identity.',['Ji2017'])
problem(22,'The degree formula after deleting finiteness',[44],'Establish exactly λ^ν sections of a degreeλ finite étale cover.','Retain finite locally free T/S; no analogous formula holds for arbitrary affine connected finite-type T.','Stacks04DY and finite Artin decomposition prove CL041; the squaring cover of Gm refutes the enlarged statement CL042.','The finiteness hypothesis is visibly deleted in one statement while later arguments still use finite local pieces.','Worth a scan and scope correction, not an unrestricted generalization.',['Stacks04DY','BLR1990'])
problem(23,'Four-condition homogeneous criterion',[45],'Prove equivalence of component constancy, finite-étale preservation and the single binary finiteness test; establish composition.','All four conditions are equivalent for finite locally free source, as proved in proof_notes §4.','Stacks04DY and05Y8 supply the exact inputs; no first historical printed use of this homogeneous terminology was found.','The page leaves a question mark on the binary test and limits its composition assertion to the finite case.','A clean publication-history search is worthwhile; the finite-case mathematics is checked here.',['Stacks04DY','Stacks05Y8','BLR1990'])
problem(24,'Torsor restriction and the missing finite hypothesis',[47,51],'Specify when weak principal bundles become principal after restriction and determine the restricted group.','Use finite locally free T/S, represented groups/torsors and smooth surjectivity, or finite étale objects with homogeneity.','Ji2.7/5.6 plus CL019/041–046 provide the finite-source result. Pro scan55 says finite is required; Codex says without supposing finite.','The clipped transition and difficult margin make the hypothesis genuinely textually unresolved.','High priority for scan inspection; no broad nonfinite torsor theorem is inferred.',['Ji2017','Stacks04DY'])
problem(25,'Finite G-sets, internal Hom and relative components',[48,49,50],'Remove the chosen base point and prove the internal-Hom representation with étale-local compatibility.','For finite locally free homogeneous T/S construct the component quotient; do not derive it from left exactness alone or from global maps.','CL046 proves the geometric replacement using Stacks04DY. CL047 refutes the general endofunctor premise. The strictly henselian ramified quadratic example separates ordinary from internal Hom.','The earlier finite-set route is deleted; the live equivariant route explicitly leaves a compatibility check and says the base point should be unnecessary.','Worth a precise categorical exposition separating the valid geometric object from the false general premise.',['Stacks04DY','Bertapelle2016'])
problem(26,'R, DVR tests and centralizer representability',[55],'Establish R from DVR tests and from the given connected-fibre or finite-subscheme conditions, then apply it to transporters and normalizers.','State a known sufficient essential-freeness/purity hypothesis, and prove separately any equivalence with the manuscript’s R.','SGA3VIII6.1–6.7 gives closed transporter/centralizer representability under essential freeness; Murre§3B supplies the notebook’s criterion framework.','The manuscript changes hypotheses and cancels some applications; the exact equivalence is not written out.','Worth a focused comparison with purity and essential freeness, without assuming the names denote the same property.',['SGA3VIII','Murre1966'])
problem(27,'Flattening beyond the proper noetherian case',[56],'Extend the adic-effectivity flattening criterion to group/R and nonnoetherian cases and clarify faithful flatness.','Retain coherent finite-presentation data, use properness for formal effectivity, and add support/nonemptiness when asking faithful flatness.','Murre§3A Theorem2/Corollary1 exactly handles the proper locally noetherian coherent case; the other variants were not exactly matched.','The proof is an eight-condition sketch and the relevant formula has F/E ambiguity.','Worth a bounded hypothesis audit; unrestricted flattening is not inferred from the proper case.',['Murre1966','Stacks08K6'])
problem(28,'Flat self-relations and formal torsors',[57,58],'Finish representability of the image factor and the formal-principal homogeneous corollary.','Use the flat projection criterion; add flatness of G for the principal-action corollary and state finite-presentation/approximation hypotheses.','Murre§3A Corollary2 supplies the noetherian factorization theorem; CL052’s nonflat group is a complete counterexample to the unqualified corollary.','The source’s Reste is followed by further proof; scan14 omits a visible group-flatness condition.','Worth preserving as a local proof completion and a high-impact hypothesis flag.',['Murre1966'])
problem(29,'Kernel quotient and arbitrary-base approximation',[59,60],'Construct G/Ker(u) as the image scheme and justify the coherent tangent-module base-change/open-locus machinery.','For the quotient retain flat fp kernel and fp map; for tangent modules retain proper flat fp source and coherent fp coefficients. Separate noetherian theorem from approximation.','Murre§3A application after Corollary2 and Stacks08JY/08K6 are the exact available results.','The notebook invokes finite-presentation approximation and Nakayama tersely; no evidence of an abandoned theorem is supplied.','Useful technical commentary, but not a new research direction under the checked hypotheses.',['Murre1966','Stacks08JY','Stacks08K6'])


def write_tsv(path,fields,rows):
    with path.open('w',newline='') as f:
        w=csv.DictWriter(f,fieldnames=fields,delimiter='\t');w.writeheader();w.writerows(rows)
def serialize():
    for name,data in [('claims',claims),('problems',problems)]:
        (R/(name+'.json')).write_text(json.dumps(data,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\n')
    write_tsv(R/'search_log.tsv',list(searches[0]),searches)
    if reads:write_tsv(R/'readings.tsv',list(reads[0]),reads)
    if links:write_tsv(R/'links.tsv',list(links[0]),links)
    bs=[]
    for r in refs:
        fields={'title':r['title'],'author':r['author'],'url':r['url'],'urldate':DATE,'note':r['note'],'annote':r['loc']+'. '+r['detail']}
        if r['year']:fields['year']=r['year']
        bs.append('@misc{'+r['key']+',\n'+',\n'.join('  '+k+' = {'+str(v).replace('&','\\&')+'}' for k,v in fields.items())+'\n}\n')
    (R/'references.bib').write_text('\n'.join(bs))
    old=list(csv.DictReader((R/'CHECK_EVENTS.tsv').open(),delimiter='\t'))
    base=[e for e in old if e['statement_id'].startswith('SA03-')]
    reference_events=[dict(statement_id=r['key'],date=DATE,who=WHO,type='used and rechecked in this run' if r['note']=='verified' else 'carried as background without fault found',outcome=('Opened link; compared stated locator/hypotheses. '+r['detail']) if r['note']=='verified' else ('Access not verified; not used as proof authority. '+r['detail'])) for r in refs]
    write_tsv(R/'CHECK_EVENTS.tsv',['statement_id','date','who','type','outcome'],base+events+reference_events)
    print(json.dumps({'claims':len(claims),'problems':len(problems),'readings':len(reads),'links':len(links),'references':len(refs),'search_groups':len(searches),'claim_check_events':len(events)},indent=2))

if __name__=='__main__':serialize()


